 about the impeachment of Bill  Clinton  well that impeachment starts in 1994  even though it didn't resolve until 1999  in the Clinton proceedings Kenneth Starr  was appointed as independent counsel in  August of 1994 with the approval of  Attorney General Janet Reno in the wake  of the Nixon impeachment the special  prosecutor statutes were replaced with  the Independent Counsel statutes later  on so Kenneth Starr was appointed in  1994 to investigate what's called the  whitewater affair which are certain real  estate related allegations related to  when Clinton was in private practice and  although Kenneth Starr was appointed to  investigate the whitewater affair the  investigation broadened over time to  include a number of different things  including the death of Vince foster the  firing of certain White House travel  office personnel potential abuse of  confidential FBI files and eventually  the Paula Jones lawsuit and eventually  the possible perjury and obstruction of  justice to cover-up President Clinton's  sexual relationship with Monica Lewinsky  and to this day part of the controversy  over the Starr investigation is that it  started regarding the whitewater issue  but ballooned into including something  else entirely over the course of five to  six years and took on subsequent  controversies as they came up now  roughly at the same time in 1994 Paula  Jones filed suit and accused President  Clinton of sexual harassment when he was  governor  Arkansas Clinton attempted to delay the  trial the civil trial over the Paula  Jones lawsuit until after he left office  but in May of 1997 the Supreme Court  unanimously rejected Clinton's claim  that the Constitution immunized him from  civil lawsuits and shortly thereafter  pretrial discovery commenced in the  Paula Jones lawsuit as part of the Paula  Jones lawsuit in January of 1998 Clinton  gave a deposition in the Jones  litigation where he denied having a  sexual relationship with Monica Lewinsky  I've never had sexual relations with  Monica Lewinsky I never had an affair  with her a few months later in August of  1998 President Clinton testified in  front of a grand jury convened by the  Office of Independent Counsel ie  Kenneth Starr and actually testified for  four hours about his relationship with  Monica Lewinsky and whether he had  perjured himself before I knew that in  the face of their illegal activity I  still had to behave lawfully but I  wanted to be legal without being  particularly helpful you might have  heard of the famous testimony of  President Clinton where he says it  depends on what your definition of is is  well this is where it comes from from  the testimony in front of the grand jury  in 1998 a few months later in September  of 1998 Kenneth Starr and the office of  independent counsel concluded its four  year-long investigation of the president  soon after the president's grand jury  testimony and delivered the famous Starr  report to the House Judiciary Committee  the Starr report itself was extensive it  was 453 pages long  Republican House leaders argued for the  reports immediate release via the  internet which was new at the time while  the Democrats tried to delay to allow  the White House time to form a response  but after two days of debate on  September 11th 1998 the House voted in a  huge majority to release the report to  the public after which formal  impeachment of President Clinton started  in October of 1998 really just a month  after the Star report came out just a  few months later in December of 1998 the  House voted to impeach President  Clinton and in January of 1999 the  Senate began its trial of President  Clinton in February of 1999 the Senate  began taking closed-door depositions of  witnesses and in that same month the  Senate voted 70 to 30 that excerpting  the videotapes of these closed-door  depositions would suffice as testimony  rather than calling live witnesses to  appear at trial and then famously Bill  Clinton w